    "chapter_name": "Center of Mass Momentum and Collision",
    "year": "2023",
    "shift": "shift_1"
  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn></math> balls each of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> moving with speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math> simultaneously strike a wall normally and reflected back with same speed, in time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>. The total force exerted by the balls on the wall is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>200</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0029_b51a73c24c84.png\" style=\"width: 304px; height: 250px;\" />.</p><p>Force exerted by each ball is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>, here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math>&nbsp;is momentum and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math>&nbsp;is time.</p><p>So, for one ball&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>m</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>Now, total force exerted by the balls on the wall is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>200</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac></math>.</p>"
  }
}